00:45:19,090 --> 00:45:19,430
Aha.

385
00:45:20,720 --> 00:45:28,320
well, I think you know, we're gonna have much better language understanding and much better speech recognition than we do even today.

386
00:45:28,400 --> 00:45:32,240
And so products that are built around those kinds of facilities are going to be important.

387
00:45:32,320 --> 00:45:41,636
I think robotics and sort of self-driving cars, if you think of them as very big robots, are going to be emerging as really viable things in that time frame.

388
00:45:45,230 --> 00:45:46,400
one more question.

389
00:45:48,366 --> 00:45:49,796
I guess it's a long question.

390
00:45:50,030 --> 00:45:55,040
There are many libraries for machine learning, such as a cafe, CNO, MaxNet.

391
00:45:55,374 --> 00:45:58,340
What are the distinguishing advantages of TensorFlow?

392
00:45:59,246 --> 00:46:04,880
So I think we view TensorFlow as something that is good on three attributes.

393
00:46:05,038 --> 00:46:14,436
It's good on expressibility, so it's easy to express pretty much the vast majority of modern machine learning research algorithms using TensorFlow.

394
00:46:14,960 --> 00:46:24,400
It's good on scalability, so you can essentially take it and train on large data sets, and it's portable, so you can have a variety of different ways in which you use it.

395
00:46:24,494 --> 00:46:42,960
You can train it on our CloudML product, you can train it on a desktop machine with lots of GPU cards that you've set up yourself, you can train it on a large data center, you can deploy it in any of those settings or on mobile phones, or on sort of new emerging kinds of specialized hardware for machine learning.

396
00:46:43,040 --> 00:46:48,720
And I think you know that flexibility and expressibility and scalability are what distinguish TensorFlow.

397
00:46:49,358 --> 00:46:49,572
